# Cloudflare Pages: the dashboard is a set of plain files with no build step,
# so a cached copy of one script can leave the site running a mix of old and
# new code. "no-cache" does not mean "never store" — the browser may keep the
# file, but it must check with the server before reusing it, so a push shows up
# on the next load instead of whenever the cache happens to expire.

/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
